<%- include('partials/header') %>

<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Privacy policy</div>
    <span class="eyebrow hero__eyebrow">Your privacy</span>
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>How <%= SITE.name %> collects, uses and protects your personal information.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="prose" style="max-width:800px;">
      <p class="muted">Last updated: <%= updated %>.</p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p><%= SITE.legalName || SITE.name %> ("we", "us")<%= SITE.companyNumber ? ', a company registered in England and Wales (no. ' + SITE.companyNumber + ')' : '' %>, is the data controller for the personal information described here.<%= SITE.icoNumber ? ' We are registered with the Information Commissioner’s Office under number ' + SITE.icoNumber + '.' : '' %> Contact us at <a href="mailto:<%= SITE.email %>"><%= SITE.email %></a>, on <%= SITE.phone %>, or by post at <%= SITE.address %>.</p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Enquiries, callback requests and visit bookings:</strong> your name, phone number and/or email, the home you’re interested in, the type of care, when suits you, and anything you write in your message. If you tell us about someone’s health or care needs, we hold that too.</li>
        <li><strong>Job applications and careers questions:</strong> your name, contact details, the role, your answer about your right to work in the UK, your message and any CV you upload.</li>
        <li><strong>Residents and people we’re assessing:</strong> the health, care and next-of-kin information we need to assess and provide care. This is gathered in person, not through this website.</li>
        <li><strong>Our chat assistant:</strong> the questions you type into it (see section 6).</li>
        <li><strong>Our staff:</strong> if you work for us and use our staff hub, your name, work email, job title, the homes you work at, a work phone number if you add one, your photo if you choose to upload one, your training certificates, and a record of changes you make in the hub.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical information:</strong> our servers keep short-lived logs (such as IP address and pages requested) to keep the site running and secure.</li>
        <li><strong>Visitor statistics:</strong> we count which pages are viewed, the website that sent you here, your type of device and what you search for on Find a home. To count each visitor once a day, your IP address and browser details are scrambled into a code that changes every day; your IP address itself isn’t stored, and we can’t use the code to identify you. No cookies are used.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Why we use it, and our lawful basis</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Answering enquiries and arranging visits:</strong> our legitimate interest in helping people find care, and taking steps you’ve asked for before any contract. Health information you share is used to provide health and social care.</li>
        <li><strong>Recruitment:</strong> taking steps before a possible employment contract, and our legal duty to check the right to work in the UK.</li>
        <li><strong>Caring for residents:</strong> our contract with the resident or their funder, and the provision of health and social care, with the confidentiality that requires.</li>
        <li><strong>Running our staff hub:</strong> the employment relationship and our legitimate interest in running our homes. Staff photos are used only with the person’s consent, which they can withdraw at any time by removing the photo.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal and regulatory duties:</strong> for example, records the Care Quality Commission requires.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>Only with people who need it: health and care professionals involved in someone’s care (such as GPs, district nurses and hospitals), local authorities and the NHS, and our regulators such as the Care Quality Commission. We also use service providers who handle data on our behalf and only on our instructions:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>our website hosting, database and secure file storage providers (we use Supabase for our database and file storage);</li>
        <li>our email provider (Resend), which delivers emails such as visit confirmations and staff sign-in links;</li>
        <li>our chat assistant provider (Anthropic), which receives only what you type into the chat.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Some of these providers may process data outside the UK. Where they do, we make sure the transfer is protected by safeguards recognised under UK law. We never sell your data.</p>

      <h2>5. How long we keep it</h2>
      <% if (retentionDays) { %><p><strong>Job applications</strong>, including any CV, are deleted automatically <%= retentionDays %> days after you apply, unless you join us or we have a legal reason to keep them longer.</p><% } else { %><p><strong>Job applications</strong>, including any CV, are kept only as long as we need them for recruitment, then deleted.</p><% } %>
      <p><strong>Enquiries and visit bookings</strong> are kept while we’re helping you and for a reasonable time afterwards, so we can pick up where we left off if you come back to us.</p>
      <p><strong>Staff hub accounts</strong> are deleted when someone leaves, along with their photo and certificates. A record of changes made in the hub is kept for accountability.</p>
      <p><strong>Residents’ care records</strong> are kept for as long as the law and care regulations require.</p>
      <p>CVs, certificates and staff photos are stored privately: they can only be opened by members of our team who are signed in, and are never published.</p>

      <h2>6. Our chat assistant</h2>
      <p>The chat assistant on this website answers questions using the information published on the site. What you type is sent to our provider, Anthropic, to produce the reply. We don’t save chat conversations. Please don’t type in health details or other sensitive information — call us instead and we’ll be glad to talk it through.</p>

      <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
      <p>Under UK data protection law you can ask to see the information we hold about you, have it corrected or deleted, restrict or object to how we use it, and receive a copy to take elsewhere. Where we rely on your consent, you can withdraw it at any time. To do any of these, contact us using the details above.</p>
      <p>If you ask what we hold about you, we’ll send a complete copy. If you ask us to delete it, we permanently delete every application, enquiry and visit booking linked to your email address or phone number, including any CV. We reply within one month, as the law requires.</p>

      <h2>8. Complaints</h2>
      <p>If you have a concern, please tell us first and we’ll try to put it right. You can also complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a> or on 0303 123 1113.</p>

      <h2>9. Changes</h2>
      <p>We update this notice when the way we use information changes. The date at the top shows when it was last updated.</p>

      <p style="margin-top:2rem;"><a href="/cookies" class="care-card__link">See our cookie policy →</a></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
